                %li
                  %a{:href => "#equivariant_refinement"} Equivariant refinement
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesGeometricRefinement"} Geometric refinement
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Recall that
            %em geometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            is an operation acting on tuples roughly consisting of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                with the structure of a torus-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^n \to X \to X/T^n
                – modelling
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %li
              %p
                equipped with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 2-bundle with connection
                – modelling the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kalb-Ramond+field"} Kalb-Ramond field
            %li
              %p
                and in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
                refined to elements in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential twisted K-theory
                – modelling the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            %li
              %p
                and notably equipped with a (pseudo)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
                – modelling the field of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
          %p
            The idea of
            %strong topological T-duality
            (due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BouwknegtEvslinMathai04"} Bouwknegt-Evslin-Mathai 04
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#BouwknegtHannabusMathai04"} Bouwknegt-Hannabus-Mathai 04
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            and the connection and study the remaining “topological” structure.
          %p
            While the idea of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            originates in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %p
            In the language of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bi-brane"} bi-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+transform"} integral transform
            (on sheaves of sections of, or K-classes of) (twisted) vector bundles is essentially the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier-Mukai+transformation"} Fourier-Mukai transformation
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#SarkissianSchweigert08"} Sarkissian-Schweigert 08
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Two tuples
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_i \to B, G_i)_{i = 1,2}
            consisting of a
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
            over a manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            and a line
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"} bundle gerbe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_i \to X_i
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are
            %strong topological T-duals
            if there exists an isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            of the two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes"} bundle gerbes
            pulled back to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            space
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1 \times_B X_2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
